1
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:50,959
We're trying to get to Skull Island,

2
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:53,559
I'm heading there myself.

3
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:54,720
If you don't mind,

4
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:57,040
<i>you're welcome to travel with me.</i>

5
00:02:58,640 --> 00:03:00,679
<i>I have a plan.</i>

6
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,639
<i>A plan to get Mr. Man</i>

7
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:05,079
to hand over
his money and treasures to us.

8
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:08,959
Greed will lead them to their deaths
without them even realizing it.

9
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:10,200
Hey?!

10
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,759
Ghosts! Ghosts!

11
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:14,640
No!

12
00:03:21,800 --> 00:03:22,720
Whoa.

13
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:28,400
Pat. Pat. Pat.

14
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:30,839
Let's get out of here, Pat.

15
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:33,559
There are ghosts all over the island.

16
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:35,000
Let's run, Pat. Look.

17
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:39,080
Pat, look!

18
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,280
Let's run, Pat!

19
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,840
Hey.

20
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:48,120
You.

21
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:15,999
Hurry up, everyone.

22
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,079
Let's make some noise and scare
Rahu away before he swallows the moon.

23
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:28,880
Hurry up.

24
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:33,800
Wait.

25
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:35,959
Go back inside.

26
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,440
Why?

27
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:41,040
The moonlight during Rahu's eclipse

28
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:43,719
carries dark energy.

29
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,200
You shouldn't be outside watching it.

30
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:48,839
It may bring harmful forces upon you.

31
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,680
Take your child inside.

32
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,759
What's going on?

33
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:01,239
This man says there's some bad energy

34
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:03,040
and wants me to take our child inside.

35
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:05,399
Are you crazy?

36
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:08,079
Everyone's helping make noise

37
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:10,640
to scare Rahu away.

38
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:13,279
Ignore him. Come on.

39
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,399
- Come help me.
- Let's go.

40
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:16,319
- Let's go.
- He must be from somewhere else.

41
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,440
- Let's go.
- Come.

42
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,119
Come help me.

43
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,599
Alright.

44
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,199
Come on.

45
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,119
Help me.

46
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:25,360
- Come on.
- Hit it and make some noise.

47
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:57,720
The time has come.

48
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,080
Time for what?

49
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:04,600
Time for your real surprise.

50
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:18,440
It's a lunar eclipse.

51
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,440
Well.

52
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:23,640
It's such a wonderful night.

53
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:29,120
Yes, it really is a wonderful night.

54
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,560
I've been wondering

55
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:37,200
what this bed was for.

56
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,960
But I know now.

57
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:43,279
You prepared it

58
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:46,640
for me to lie here and watch the eclipse.

59
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,600
Please.

60
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,120
Thank you.

61
00:06:56,320 --> 00:07:00,760
Aren't you going to sit with me?

62
00:07:02,560 --> 00:07:06,040
This spot is not for me.

63
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,600
Then who is it for?

64
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,440
Pat! Pat!

65
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,199
Pat, let's run!

66
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,360
They're ghosts!

67
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:20,440
Pat, let's run. They're ghosts.

68
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:25,559
Are you drunk, Win?
What nonsense are you talking about?

69
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:27,599
I'm not drunk. They're ghosts.

70
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:30,399
They tricked us.
There aren't any treasures.

71
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,719
They're ghosts! Let's run!

72
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:35,120
Stop talking nonsense.
I think you're drunk.

73
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:40,000
I'm sorry, Mr. Man.

74
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:51,320
Playtime is over.

75
00:07:51,920 --> 00:07:53,080
What is this?!

76
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:25,200
The time has come
to begin my final ritual.

77
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:31,040
You're not human!

78
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,159
Realizing it now is too late.

79
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:40,360
Your greed for another person's treasure

80
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:45,280
has brought you to this miserable end.

81
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:49,519
Please let me go.
I don't want anything anymore.

82
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:52,879
I don't want to die. Please let me go.

83
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:53,880
Please let me go.

84
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:56,359
I don't want to die either.

85
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:59,640
If you let me go,
I'll leave this island immediately.

86
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:39,759
Win! Do something!

87
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:41,679
He's going to kill us.

88
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:44,840
What do you expect me to do?
I can't even move!

89
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,159
Just do something.
Are you just going to lie there?

90
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:49,119
We're going to die!

91
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:51,560
This is all your fault!

92
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:54,199
You're the one who dragged me here to die!

93
00:09:54,200 --> 00:09:55,600
Shut up.

94
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:57,720
Men is performing a ritual.

95
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,520
He needs silence.

96
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:01,800
The next person who opens their mouth

97
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:04,160
will die first.

98
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:15,319
Please don't kill me. I don't want to die!

99
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,039
Please don't kill me. I don't want to die.

100
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:19,199
Kill her. She planned everything.

101
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,360
Kill her!

102
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:22,439
Win!

103
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:24,760
Kill her. It's all her plan.

104
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,799
No, please. I'm scared.

105
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:29,320
Please don't.

106
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:34,160
Please don't kill me. I'm scared.

107
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:41,720
No, please.

108
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,080
No.

109
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:55,480
Stop committing sins, Men.

110
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:18,360
You again? We finally met again.

111
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:21,800
But I don't have time to play with you.

112
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,360
No! Don't!

113
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,240
Help me.

114
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,560
Help me.

115
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:17,160
No, please.

116
00:13:59,960 --> 00:14:02,839
I have successfully completed
the sacrifice of the final two lives.

117
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:05,880
From this day forward,
I will become what I once was.

118
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:20,120
You can't escape me.

119
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:39,040
Venerable Sir!

120
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,120
Kang.

121
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:45,400
What's wrong?

122
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:49,280
You must've been dreaming
about the Venerable Sir.

123
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:52,400
Yes, I saw him in my dream.

124
00:14:55,960 --> 00:15:00,040
What happened in your dream?
Why were you shouting like that?

125
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:02,479
I saw him

126
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:04,680
drowning.

127
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,920
He was about to die.

128
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:19,360
It's nothing, Kang. It was only a dream.

129
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:25,240
You probably miss him very much,
that's why you dreamed about him.

130
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:33,120
What are you doing?

131
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:36,519
I'm going to pray and dedicate merit

132
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:39,079
to the guardian spirits
protecting the Venerable Sir.

133
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:41,479
Maybe they'll keep him safe.

134
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:43,520
Then I'll pray with you.

135
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,960
Me too.

136
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:48,720
Thank you.

137
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,680
Thank you,

138
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,520
Kang.

139
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:55,639
I will continue my ritual
for three days and three nights

140
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:57,480
without leaving this room.

141
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,199
You're responsible
for maintaining order on the island.

142
00:17:00,200 --> 00:17:02,240
Kill anyone who enters.

143
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,359
Yes.

144
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:10,720
In a few more days, I will finally settle
the matter I've been waiting for.

145
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:37,600
- Your coffee.
- Thank you.

146
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:40,839
I'll help, Mom.

147
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:42,920
Thank you, sweetie.

148
00:17:45,280 --> 00:17:46,640
Where did you go yesterday?

149
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:51,000
Mook.

150
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:54,480
Why are you just standing there?
Answer your dad.

151
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:58,039
Mook went to the beach with me, Dad.

152
00:17:58,040 --> 00:18:00,799
Na, here you are. Want some coffee?

153
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:02,279
Yes, please. Thank you, Mom.

154
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:03,480
Alright.

155
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:10,519
Na, you spend more time
by the sea than at home.

156
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:12,999
Aren't you tired of it yet?

157
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:15,719
I am, but Dara isn't.

158
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:17,480
So I asked Mook to come along too.

159
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:20,760
Just the three of you?

160
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:23,800
There was another friend too.

161
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:26,600
We also stopped by the beach house.

162
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:31,720
I know. I was just asking.

163
00:18:33,040 --> 00:18:34,360
How did you know, Dad?

164
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:36,000
Oh?

165
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:40,440
If someone enters my house
and I don't know, that would be terrible.

166
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:42,639
These days, there are
so many thieves and criminals.

167
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:44,919
So I asked some people around there
to keep an eye on the house for me.

168
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:47,199
They called and told me. I already figured

169
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:50,399
it had to be Na, Da, and you.

170
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:53,039
I was just wondering
who the other person was.

171
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:55,600
If you say it was your friend,
then it's alright.

172
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:05,679
That was close.

173
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,240
Good thing we told the truth.

174
00:19:08,320 --> 00:19:11,280
But we still lied to Dad
about your friend.

175
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:14,759
Well, I consider Mr. Narathon

176
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:16,920
one of my friends too.

177
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:21,680
Dad didn't ask for a name,
so let's just take it as a win.

178
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:27,200
But no matter what,
Dad absolutely cannot know

179
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:30,320
that we went to contact Sarai's spirit.

180
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,199
If he finds out I'm involved
with ghosts again,

181
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:36,040
I'm dead for sure.

182
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:39,360
Alright. I know.

183
00:19:40,480 --> 00:19:43,720
So what is Mr. Narathon going to do next?

184
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:48,000
I still don't know.

185
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:54,000
I suggest going to the police.

186
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:56,600
Everything would be solved faster.

187
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:05,040
Yes. I'll try
talking to Mr. Narathon about it.

188
00:20:07,320 --> 00:20:08,160
Good.

189
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,720
Has Sairung already gone out?

190
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:32,840
Ms. Sairung hasn't come home
for several days.

191
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,280
Since when?

192
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:40,560
Since Mr. Phum
was admitted to the hospital.

193
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,320
Yes, Prach?

194
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:59,480
Alright. I'll meet you at the hospital.

195
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:02,040
See you.

196
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:09,320
KAIMOOK

197
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:17,480
That's enough.

198
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:19,360
Let me put it away for you.

199
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,320
Here you go.

200
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:27,000
Thank you, Kang.

201
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:31,999
Hello, Mr. Phum.

202
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,440
You look healthy today.

203
00:21:39,240 --> 00:21:42,200
Is he your son, Mr. Phum? He's adorable.

204
00:21:43,360 --> 00:21:44,320
No, he isn't.

205
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:45,760
Oh.

206
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:50,280
If you didn't tell me,
I would think he was your son.

207
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:56,920
Then, I'll take Kang out
to get something to eat first.

208
00:21:58,400 --> 00:21:59,479
Okay.

209
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:01,040
- Let's go.
- Yes.

210
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:13,600
What is this?

211
00:22:14,120 --> 00:22:17,919
I don't know either.
But for the past three or four days,

212
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:20,040
the patient has been
drawing nothing but this.

213
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:24,600
I thought it might be some kind of memory,

214
00:22:25,440 --> 00:22:27,719
so I called Professor Prachaya
to come take a look.

215
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:29,640
Maybe you might know what he means.

216
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:21,440
It's beautiful.

217
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:38,560
Beautiful...

218
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:50,240
This drawing really is beautiful.

219
00:23:53,960 --> 00:23:55,560
What is it?

220
00:24:46,320 --> 00:24:47,760
Beautiful.

221
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:54,880
Beautiful. Beautiful.

222
00:24:57,240 --> 00:25:02,040
Beautiful. Beautiful. Beautiful.

223
00:25:03,520 --> 00:25:05,160
Beautiful.

224
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:20,000
Thank you.

225
00:25:29,800 --> 00:25:31,920
Is something wrong, Mr. Narathon?

226
00:25:35,640 --> 00:25:36,960
Nothing.

227
00:25:38,680 --> 00:25:40,760
I thought we'd get something
from that drawing,

228
00:25:41,360 --> 00:25:42,640
but in the end,

229
00:25:43,560 --> 00:25:45,440
we came up empty-handed again.

230
00:25:50,120 --> 00:25:52,399
Now you know

231
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:55,280
Mr. Phum had nothing to do
with Sarai's death.

232
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:58,840
I think you should tell him about this.

233
00:26:03,080 --> 00:26:04,320
Actually,

234
00:26:06,080 --> 00:26:07,880
I've been thinking the same thing.

235
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:12,920
It's probably time Dad knew.

236
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:16,960
He has many connections.

237
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:21,800
It shouldn't be hard for him
to investigate who killed Sarai.

238
00:27:00,760 --> 00:27:02,080
Thank you.

239
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:04,720
Of course.

240
00:27:06,440 --> 00:27:07,319
I'll be right back.

241
00:27:07,320 --> 00:27:10,759
Wait. Where are you going? It's raining.

242
00:27:10,760 --> 00:27:15,440
I'm going to stand in the rain,
so I can have you wipe my face again.

243
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:20,160
Oh, come on.

244
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:29,120
I think you're too late.

245
00:27:29,640 --> 00:27:30,920
The rain just stopped.

246
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:44,920
A rainbow.

247
00:27:51,440 --> 00:27:53,280
What did Sompong try to say?

248
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:56,880
A rainbow...

249
00:27:57,880 --> 00:28:01,720
A rainbow... "Sairung"?

250
00:28:09,320 --> 00:28:11,760
Could it be Sairung, Mr. Phum's wife?

251
00:28:17,520 --> 00:28:19,960
Sairung hated Sarai.

252
00:28:21,840 --> 00:28:25,880
It's possible Sairung
had something to do with Sarai's death.

253
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:41,480
Come on, Kang. Get ready to go home.

254
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:44,560
- Are you feeling better now, Mr. Phum?
- Yes.

255
00:28:45,560 --> 00:28:47,399
What about the brain X-ray result?

256
00:28:47,400 --> 00:28:48,999
All done.

257
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:52,719
Just wait for the doctor to check
on this wound then we can go home.

258
00:28:52,720 --> 00:28:55,320
Let me go get my things
from the bathroom first.

259
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:05,240
Mr. Phum, I think I should
go back to the condo first.

260
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:11,040
That's good. I'll settle things with
Sairung first, so you can feel at ease.

261
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:16,080
What about Kang?

262
00:29:16,760 --> 00:29:17,960
What about him?

263
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:22,360
Let Kang stay with me first.
I'll take care of him.

264
00:29:23,360 --> 00:29:25,879
You really seem to have
fallen in love with Kang.

265
00:29:25,880 --> 00:29:28,400
I'm starting to get jealous of this boy.

266
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:34,640
You don't have to be jealous.
My love for you will never change.

267
00:29:37,160 --> 00:29:38,320
Really?

268
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:42,360
Yes. I love you more than my own life.

269
00:29:50,400 --> 00:29:51,760
I'm done.

270
00:29:54,560 --> 00:29:55,760
Hey.

271
00:29:56,320 --> 00:30:00,679
Next time,
spend more time in the bathroom.

272
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:03,039
But I'm already done.

273
00:30:03,040 --> 00:30:05,959
Okay. Fine.

274
00:30:05,960 --> 00:30:06,920
Come on, Kang.

275
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:09,720
- I'll help.
- Okay.

276
00:30:20,280 --> 00:30:22,760
You should have been born
as my real son, Kang.

277
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:02,519
Ms. Sairung.

278
00:31:02,520 --> 00:31:05,240
You idiot! You scared me.

279
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:07,600
Where have you been?

280
00:31:09,120 --> 00:31:11,200
Do I have to report to you
every time I go somewhere?

281
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:15,560
No. It's just that
Mr. Narathon asked about you this morning.

282
00:31:19,760 --> 00:31:21,119
What did he say?

283
00:31:21,120 --> 00:31:24,080
Nothing. He only asked where you were.

284
00:31:27,440 --> 00:31:29,879
And Mr. Phum?

285
00:31:29,880 --> 00:31:32,200
He hasn't been discharged
from the hospital yet.

286
00:31:35,480 --> 00:31:36,880
Go do whatever you need to do.

287
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:39,879
Would you like anything to eat?
I'll go to the market.

288
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:42,040
There's no fresh food left in the fridge.

289
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:47,639
That's good. Then hurry up.

290
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:49,200
I'm starving.

291
00:31:51,560 --> 00:31:52,840
Yes, ma'am.

292
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:12,720
Oh, Mr. Narathon.

293
00:32:14,360 --> 00:32:16,799
How is my father?

294
00:32:16,800 --> 00:32:19,200
Mr. Phum has already been discharged.

295
00:32:20,760 --> 00:32:21,640
Discharged?

296
00:33:29,400 --> 00:33:32,840
You sly old man.
When did you change the code?

297
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:14,679
<i>The number you are trying to reach
is currently unavailable.</i>

298
00:34:16,120 --> 00:34:17,679
Why does Dad have to turn off his phone?

299
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:21,080
Mr. Phum just left the hospital.
Maybe he forgot.

300
00:34:23,840 --> 00:34:27,238
Calm down. Didn't you tell me

301
00:34:27,239 --> 00:34:29,198
Ms. Sairung hasn't been home
for several days?

302
00:34:29,199 --> 00:34:30,120
But,

303
00:34:30,639 --> 00:34:32,560
I still don't trust that woman.

304
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:36,639
If possible, I don't want Dad
to meet her before he knows the truth.

305
00:34:38,239 --> 00:34:39,560
I'm going now.

306
00:34:40,320 --> 00:34:41,519
Wait.

307
00:34:41,520 --> 00:34:43,400
I'll follow you in my car.

308
00:34:55,840 --> 00:34:56,960
Sairung.

309
00:35:02,280 --> 00:35:03,440
Where are you going?

310
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:10,280
I asked you. Where are you going?

311
00:35:20,680 --> 00:35:22,920
When were you discharged
from the hospital?

312
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:25,480
You still haven't answered my question.

313
00:35:32,760 --> 00:35:36,959
A friend of mine is going to Hong Kong.
I'm bored at home,

314
00:35:36,960 --> 00:35:38,600
so I thought I'd go shopping with her.

315
00:35:39,200 --> 00:35:40,800
Go to Hong Kong?

316
00:35:41,960 --> 00:35:44,560
You look more like
you're running away from something.

317
00:35:47,240 --> 00:35:49,720
I'm tired of arguing with you.
I'd better go.

318
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:52,080
You killed Sarai, didn't you?

319
00:35:59,320 --> 00:36:01,640
I asked you. Did you kill Sarai?

320
00:36:32,520 --> 00:36:34,200
Why is the traffic this bad?

321
00:36:40,120 --> 00:36:41,240
Answer me.

322
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:44,840
Were you the one who ordered
those three bastards to kill Sarai?

323
00:36:52,120 --> 00:36:53,200
Yes.

324
00:37:01,680 --> 00:37:03,120
If you come any closer,

325
00:37:03,680 --> 00:37:04,840
I'll shoot.

326
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:08,880
Go ahead.

327
00:37:09,560 --> 00:37:11,000
Shoot me.

328
00:37:13,200 --> 00:37:14,479
Don't push me.

329
00:37:14,480 --> 00:37:15,760
I'm not.

330
00:37:16,720 --> 00:37:17,960
Even if I have to die,

331
00:37:18,640 --> 00:37:20,800
I won't let you get away.

332
00:37:21,680 --> 00:37:23,760
You have to pay for what you did to Sarai.

333
00:37:28,040 --> 00:37:29,560
This is why.

334
00:37:30,720 --> 00:37:33,600
It's because you loved her like this.
That's why I hated her.

335
00:37:37,160 --> 00:37:39,400
You never saw me.

336
00:37:40,360 --> 00:37:42,399
The moment she entered your life,

337
00:37:42,400 --> 00:37:45,520
you stopped caring about me.

338
00:37:48,520 --> 00:37:50,399
I hated her! Do you hear me?

339
00:37:50,400 --> 00:37:52,320
Don't use love as an excuse!

340
00:37:54,880 --> 00:37:56,640
You knew from the start
that I would never...

341
00:37:57,600 --> 00:38:00,240
I would never love
a cold-blooded woman like you.

342
00:38:03,160 --> 00:38:07,480
I know. Stop rubbing it in.

343
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:10,960
I was stupid

344
00:38:12,360 --> 00:38:14,640
for being loyal to you,

345
00:38:15,640 --> 00:38:20,160
thinking that one day
you might love me back.

346
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:27,440
But since you've finally made it clear,
that's fine.

347
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:30,840
I won't be a fool any longer.

348
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:35,680
Go upstairs.

349
00:38:47,760 --> 00:38:49,080
Now.

350
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:57,560
Go upstairs.

351
00:39:22,280 --> 00:39:23,680
What do you want?

352
00:39:25,000 --> 00:39:26,600
All the cash in the safe.

353
00:39:33,120 --> 00:39:35,039
Don't try to trick me.

354
00:39:35,040 --> 00:39:38,240
Otherwise, you'll be joining Sarai.

355
00:39:41,720 --> 00:39:42,800
Go.

356
00:40:03,600 --> 00:40:06,120
Put all the money in the bag.

357
00:40:27,240 --> 00:40:28,480
You want it so much?

358
00:40:29,880 --> 00:40:30,880
Take it.

359
00:40:32,280 --> 00:40:33,240
Hey!

360
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:43,840
Too many tricks.
You think I won't shoot you?

361
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:10,199
Do you want me to call the police?

362
00:41:10,200 --> 00:41:11,600
No.

363
00:41:12,880 --> 00:41:15,120
I'll handle this myself.

364
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:19,800
Who else was involved?

365
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:27,240
Even now, you still feel no remorse?

366
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:33,080
Who were those three bastards?

367
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,720
I asked you. Who were they?

368
00:41:46,840 --> 00:41:48,319
You want to know them?

369
00:41:48,320 --> 00:41:50,720
Don't play games with me.

370
00:41:52,680 --> 00:41:54,120
I'm not.

371
00:41:54,920 --> 00:41:57,000
If you want to meet them,

372
00:41:57,840 --> 00:41:59,480
I'll introduce you.

373
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:03,200
Mr. Narathon.

374
00:42:04,720 --> 00:42:06,120
- Hey!
- Kaimook.

375
00:42:09,000 --> 00:42:10,120
Who are you?

376
00:42:13,880 --> 00:42:15,720
One of the people you wanted to meet.

377
00:42:22,080 --> 00:42:23,360
Pong.

378
00:42:27,960 --> 00:42:30,000
He's the owner of the boat I took before.

379
00:42:37,040 --> 00:42:40,600
Let Ms. Sairung go. Or this girl dies.

380
00:42:46,560 --> 00:42:50,000
Well? Or do you want to take the risk?

381
00:43:06,120 --> 00:43:07,760
Hand the gun over to Ms. Sairung.

382
00:43:17,360 --> 00:43:18,360
Go get some rope.

383
00:43:31,040 --> 00:43:32,200
I never thought

384
00:43:32,760 --> 00:43:36,399
Mr. Phum Witassanai
would end up like this.

385
00:43:36,400 --> 00:43:38,239
That's because
I keep a snake like you in my house.

386
00:43:38,240 --> 00:43:40,080
- Mr. Phum!
- Enough.

387
00:43:41,240 --> 00:43:42,200
Let's go.

388
00:43:42,840 --> 00:43:43,800
Kaimook.

389
00:43:44,320 --> 00:43:46,400
Sorry, Mr. Narathon.

390
00:43:47,160 --> 00:43:48,920
We're taking your girlfriend with us.

391
00:43:50,040 --> 00:43:52,360
If either of you lays a finger on Kaimook,

392
00:43:52,880 --> 00:43:54,800
I won't let you live.

393
00:43:55,600 --> 00:43:58,320
How terrifying. Should I be scared?

394
00:43:59,800 --> 00:44:01,800
Trust me, Kaimook.

395
00:44:03,800 --> 00:44:08,480
I will help you.
I will come for you. I promise.

396
00:44:09,680 --> 00:44:10,759
That's enough.

397
00:44:10,760 --> 00:44:11,920
Go.

398
00:44:22,920 --> 00:44:25,719
I intended to give it
to the person I love most.

399
00:44:25,720 --> 00:44:28,360
<i>And now I've found her.</i>

400
00:44:30,760 --> 00:44:33,000
Da, help me.

401
00:44:33,520 --> 00:44:34,359
Win.

402
00:44:34,360 --> 00:44:35,719
Help me!

403
00:44:35,720 --> 00:44:37,519
Kang, Sarai,

404
00:44:37,520 --> 00:44:39,200
please forgive me.

405
00:45:18,440 --> 00:45:20,400
Subtitle translation by: Panuwat Baikeawon
